{
  "_comment": "Rank-resolved follow-up to the v2 DE grid (step 2b). Same GRN/base config/seed_base (40000)/n_replicates (8) as the v2 grid, so iid_random, constant_iid_mean and de_locked_best_v2 should reproduce the v2 results exactly for all pre-existing metrics; new arms and metrics are additive. New arms: lowrank_rank1/lowrank_rank3 (exactly rank-k states with IID-matched per-MR range; mr_state_harness.sample_lowrank_mr_states) and de_v2_column_shuffled (v2 DE matrix with MR columns permuted per replicate: preserves state geometry and per-MR marginals, destroys state-to-GRN alignment). New metrics (mr_state_harness._state_expression_rank_metrics): mr_state_expression_distance_correlation_null_mean/_null_q95/_excess (cluster/state shuffle null); centroid_n_reproducible_dims, centroid_reproducible_participation_ratio, centroid_reproducible_variance_fraction (split-half-cell reproducible between-cluster rank, noise-controlled by a label-permutation parallel-analysis null; SERGIO scenario only, NaN for the one-cell-per-cluster surrogate); state_expression_cka/_cka_null_mean/_cka_excess (state/expression Gram alignment vs. shuffle null).",
  "_comment_interpretation": "Question answered: do DE states carry high-dimensional, state-linked programs through SERGIO rather than noise-induced dimensions? Read centroid_reproducible_participation_ratio/centroid_n_reproducible_dims (expression-side, noise-controlled rank) together with state_expression_cka_excess and the correlation excess (state link). Expected: constant ~0; lowrank_rank1/3 cap near 1/3 reproducible dims with high CKA excess; IID/DE higher rank; de_v2_column_shuffled keeps the state's geometry but should lose the DE advantage in correlation/CKA excess if DE's gain is GRN-specific alignment. Interpret CKA only as excess over its own null (flat-spectrum states have a high chance level). Paired deltas are vs. iid_random. CAVEAT (smoke test): the constant arm showed 13 'reproducible' dims / 0.73 reproducible variance fraction, so centroid_* metrics must be read as excess over constant_iid_mean, not as absolute state-linked rank; correlation and CKA excess are the state-linked readouts.",
